    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm looking at a 2022 Ford F-150 that's slipping under load. I'm running a diagnostic scan and I'm seeing some really irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit. What are the most likely culprits for these kind of fluctuations in an automatic transmission?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most likely culprits for irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit of a 2022 Ford F-150 automatic transmission are faulty solenoids, leaky seals or hoses, or a clogged or dirty pump filter. Solenoid failure can cause erratic pressure spikes, while seals or hoses that are damaged or worn can lead to fluid leaks, affecting transmission performance. Clogged or dirty pump filters can also cause transmission shifting issues.",
